#. Tag: title
#: tutorial.docbook:11
#, no-c-format
msgid "Step by Step Tutorial"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: primary
#: tutorial.docbook:12
#, no-c-format
msgid "tutorial"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:13
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This section is a step by step walk through of the most important functions "
"needed to understand how to create and manipulate a complex document. This "
"tutorial will generate the start of a newsletter as an example document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:18
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is recommend that you go through the tutorial in order at least once if "
"you are new to frame based word processors."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tutorial.docbook:22
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tutorial: Choosing the initial template"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:24
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The steps to this tutorial are numbered from 1 to 23. Beneath each step, is "
"text in <emphasis>italics</emphasis> which further elaborates or explains "
"the changes."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:27
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you first <link linkend=\"starting-kword\">start &kword;</link> (or "
"<link linkend=\"new-doc\">start a new document</link> after &kword; is "
"running), &kword; asks for a document template."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: phrase
#: tutorial.docbook:33 tutorial.docbook:52 tutorial.docbook:63
#: tutorial.docbook:72 tutorial.docbook:112 tutorial.docbook:129
#: tutorial.docbook:136 tutorial.docbook:166 tutorial.docbook:173
#: tutorial.docbook:199 tutorial.docbook:207 tutorial.docbook:221
#: tutorial.docbook:233 tutorial.docbook:256 tutorial.docbook:268
#: tutorial.docbook:274 tutorial.docbook:282 tutorial.docbook:288
#: tutorial.docbook:297 tutorial.docbook:305 tutorial.docbook:320
#: tutorial.docbook:330
#, no-c-format
msgid "Screen shot"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:36
#, no-c-format
msgid "Here you can either:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:39
#, no-c-format
msgid "Select the initial template for your new document."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:43
#, no-c-format
msgid "Open a &kword; document saved to your hard drive or network."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:49
#, no-c-format
msgid "Step 1: Click on <guilabel>Page Layout</guilabel>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:54
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will list the Page Layout templates available on your system. For "
"information on the differences between Page Layout and Text Oriented "
"templates, see the section entitled <link linkend=\"wp-vs-dtp\">The "
"difference between Text Oriented and Page Layout templates</link>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:59
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Step 2: Now select the <guilabel>Simple Layout</guilabel> icon by clicking "
"once with the left button of your mouse."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:65
#, no-c-format
msgid "<emphasis>This is the template we will use for the tutorial</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:68
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Step 3: Now confirm your selection by clicking on <guibutton>Use This "
"Template</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:74
#, no-c-format
msgid "<emphasis>To complete your selection</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:76
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"&kword; will open a new document with three frames. The frames are outlined "
"on the white background, as gray boxes. Each box is a separate frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tutorial.docbook:83
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tutorial: Selecting a frame and entering text into that frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:85
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"To begin entering text (or adding any sort of data for that matter) into a "
"document, its important to let &kword; know which frame to put the data in."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:90
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"In order to keep both editing and formatting of your document efficient and "
"simple, the command executed with a mouse click changes depending on where "
"in the &kword; window the pointer is located."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:94
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the pointer is located over toolbars, scrollbars, menu buttons or other "
"areas <emphasis>outside the document</emphasis>, the pointer is an arrow. "
"You should already be familiar with this type of pointer when using other "
"&kde; programs."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:97
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When <emphasis>inside the document</emphasis>, there are two separate "
"pointers which alternate automatically based on how close to a frame edge "
"the pointer is currently located."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:99
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When the mouse pointer is near the edge of a frame, the pointer will change "
"into two intersecting lines with arrows on all four points. Clicking the "
"left mouse button now will select the nearest frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:101
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"As you move the pointer away from the edge of the frame, the pointer will "
"change into the text entry pointer. Clicking the left mouse button at this "
"time will tell &kword; to insert text into this frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:106
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Step 4: Place the mouse pointer over the upper-left frame. Make sure you do "
"not see the <emphasis>frame select pointer</emphasis>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:108
#, no-c-format
msgid "Step 5: Click once with the left mouse button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:114
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This tells &kword; to insert text into this frame. Click in the upper left "
"corner of the frame to position the cursor in the upper left corner of the "
"frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:116
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Step 6: Enter the following text using the keyboard: <userinput>KWord Press "
"Release</userinput>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:118
#, no-c-format
msgid "This is some sample text for our newsletter."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:121
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Step 7: Select <emphasis>KWord Press Release</emphasis> by placing the mouse "
"cursor on the right end of the text. Click once with the &LMB; and drag the "
"mouse cursor to the left. Selected text will be white text on a colored "
"background. When all the text has been selected, release the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:130
#, no-c-format
msgid "This defines what text is going to be altered with Step 8."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:131
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Step 8: Click inside the <guilabel>Text Size</guilabel> combo box. Change "
"this number to 26."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:138
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This changes the size of the selected text to one more appropriate for a "
"title."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tutorial.docbook:143
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tutorial: Changing the size of a frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:145
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now that we have entered some text, we can see that the frame should extend "
"across the entire width of the page for a title. We need to change the size "
"and shape of the frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:149
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Step 9: Place the mouse pointer over the frame border (you will notice the "
"cursor changes to two intersecting lines with arrows), and click once with "
"the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:153
#, no-c-format
msgid "This will select this frame, so it can be re-shaped."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:156
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"You will now notice the frame is outlined in black, with 8 squares on the "
"outline. These squares are used for re-sizing the frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:160
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Step 10: Place the mouse pointer over the square in the lower right corner "
"of the frame. Click with the &LMB; and hold it down. Drag the mouse up and "
"to the right."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:168
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Notice how the frame changes shape. Adjust the size and shape of the frame "
"until it looks similar to the example below:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:175
#, no-c-format
msgid "When it does, release the mouse button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tutorial.docbook:180
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tutorial: Moving a frame on the page and layering frames"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:182
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now that we have created a title block, we will center it at the top of the "
"page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:185
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Step 11: Place the mouse pointer over the border of the frame (but not on "
"any of the squares)."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:188
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The pointer will now change to a 4 way arrow. This indicates &kword; is "
"ready to move the frame on the page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:192
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Step 12: Click and hold with the &LMB;. Drag the mouse, and the frame will "
"follow it. Position the frame in the center of the page near the top. When "
"you are satisfied with its final location, release the mouse button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:201
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Notice how the right side of the title block has slid behind the empty frame "
"on the right. This is easily corrected."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:203
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Step 13: Select <menuchoice><guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Bring to "
"Front</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:209
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"This will place the title on top of the other frame. You can raise and lower "
"frames to give you the look you need."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tutorial.docbook:213
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tutorial: Adding a new frame/Making text flow between two frames"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:214
#, no-c-format
msgid "Now we will add a new text frame to our document for our first article."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:215
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Step 14: Begin by selecting <menuchoice><guimenu>Insert</"
"guimenu><guimenuitem>Text Frame</guimenuitem></menuchoice> from the menubar."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:223
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The pointer has changed to cross-hairs. You can draw your new text box with "
"this cursor. Start by placing the pointer at one corner. Click and hold the "
"<mousebutton>left</mousebutton> mouse button. Drag the mouse diagonally. An "
"outline will appear which represents your new text frame. When you have a "
"text frame of reasonable size, release the <mousebutton>left</mousebutton> "
"mouse button."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:235
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"It is not important if your text box does not resemble the example for the "
"purposes of this tutorial."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:238
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"When you release the <mousebutton>left</mousebutton> mouse button, a new "
"dialog box appears."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:242
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"<emphasis>This dialog box lists all the current frame sets and has a radio "
"button to create a new frame set (default value). By selecting the default "
"value, you will create a new frame set (text will not flow from any other "
"frame into this frame)</emphasis>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:247
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Notice that the default name for this frameset is <guilabel>Text Frameset 3</"
"guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:250
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Step 15: For the purposes of this tutorial, the default value of "
"<guilabel>Create a new frameset</guilabel> is good. Simply select "
"<guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:258
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now you can see your new frame has been created. It is called <guilabel>Text "
"Frameset 3</guilabel>"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:261
#, no-c-format
msgid "Now we are going to create another small frame right next to this one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:263
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Step 16: Select <menuchoice><guimenu>Insert</guimenu><guimenuitem>Text "
"Frame</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:270
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Again using the crosshair pointer, draw another small frame near the first "
"one."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:276
#, no-c-format
msgid "A dialog box will appear."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:278
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Step 17: Select <guilabel>Text Frameset 3</guilabel> by clicking with the "
"&LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:284
#, no-c-format
msgid "Step 18: Select <guibutton>OK</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:290
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"What you have just done, is connect this new textframe, to the last frame "
"you created. To test this:"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:293
#, no-c-format
msgid "Step 19: Click once inside the leftmost frame with the &LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:299
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Step 20: Begin typing. You will need to type quite a bit, but keep typing. "
"When you run out of space in the text frame, you will see your new text is "
"moved immediately into your new text frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tutorial.docbook:310
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tutorial: Deleting a frame"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:312
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Now we will delete an unneeded frame. We will delete the long text frame on "
"the right side of the page."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:315
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Step 21: Place the mouse pointer over the frame border of the right hand "
"text frame (Remember: watch for the pointer to change), and click with the "
"&LMB;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:322
#, no-c-format
msgid "This selects the frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:324
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Step 22: Select <menuchoice><guimenu>Frames</guimenu><guimenuitem>Delete "
"Frame</guimenuitem></menuchoice>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:332
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"A small dialog box appears, checking that you really intended to delete this "
"frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:333
#, no-c-format
msgid "Step 23: Select <guibutton>Delete</guibutton>."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: emphasis
#: tutorial.docbook:335
#, no-c-format
msgid "This deletes the frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: title
#: tutorial.docbook:339
#, no-c-format
msgid "Tutorial: Summary"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:341
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"Hopefully this tutorial has introduced you to the most basic tasks in "
"&kword;."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:343
#, no-c-format
msgid "At this point, you have :"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:346
#, no-c-format
msgid "Started a new document using a template"
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:347
#, no-c-format
msgid "Added text to a frame."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:348
#, no-c-format
msgid "Resized text."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:349
#, no-c-format
msgid "Created, moved, resized and deleted frames."
msgstr ""

#. Tag: para
#: tutorial.docbook:351
#, no-c-format
msgid ""
"The purpose of this tutorial was not to explore every aspect of &kword;, but "
"to introduce you to the bare essentials. Hopefully you understand the basic "
"manipulation of frames. From this point, you can refer to the specific "
"sections of the manual for help, tips and advanced features of &kword;."
msgstr ""
